      '\n' +
      '## Purpose\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This document is the durable bidirectional requirements-to-architecture-to-code-\n' +
      'to-verification matrix. It implements the Requirements Recovery Principle in\n' +
      "`docs/01-product-charter.md` without treating Copperfin's existing behavior as\n" +
      'its own requirement source. The historical filename remains stable because\n' +
      'recovered compatibility requirements are one important subset of this matrix.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Allowed requirement evidence is limited to observed behavior from a real,\n' +
      'installed VFP9 environment, shipped Microsoft/VFP documentation, explicit\n' +
      'repository-owner product policy, and registered known-bug or crash exceptions\n' +
      'in `docs/27-known-vfp9-bug-exceptions.md`.\n' +
      'Decompiled or disassembled VFP binaries are prohibited inputs under\n' +
      '`docs/07-clean-room-rules.md`.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Existing Copperfin implementation and tests may confirm or contradict a\n' +
      'requirement, but may not originate one. A derived requirement must identify its\n' +
      'parent product requirement or hazard. When allowed evidence and implementation\n' +
      'disagree, use `gap` or `exception`; never rewrite the requirement to describe\n' +
      'whatever the code happens to do.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Assurance Boundary\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Copperfin's DO-178C-inspired discipline is adapted to a general-purpose\n" +
